why: persistence audit lane 5 of 7: one Sql = one connection, no pool
  anywhere; the first service with more than one request needs one.

what: okay.sql.Pool[C <: Sql](size, acquire timeout)(open, close):
  borrow (a program on one connection, back after, through the brake),
  pinned (a Resource-scoped connection), stats, close; single-cell
  TRef state, waiters as callbacks, cancel-safe hand-off; Hikari is
  open = () => JdbcSql(ds.getConnection). Tests on H2.

